# Build artifacts
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# CMake out-of-source build
build/
cmake-build-*/

# Which mode the objects were built in; see the Makefile, .build-mode.
.build-mode

# Test and example executables (carry the _cpp suffix, per the coding convention)
*_cpp

# Hand-made diffs and patches. One was committed by accident on 2026-08-09, which is what a
# scratch file with no rule against it eventually is.
*.diff
*.patch

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python (the prototype twins in experiments/ordering; see CLAUDE.md, Tooling).
# No pyproject.toml and no venv today, the layers being stdlib-only scripts run
# by a bare python3, but bytecode appears as soon as one is run, and .venv/ would
# appear if a dependency ever arrives and the folder becomes a uv project.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# clangd compile database (machine-specific: absolute paths, local toolchain).
# Regenerate with `bear -- make test`; see CLAUDE.md, Tooling / Editor navigation.
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# The vendored ordering codes (SuiteSparse AMD, Sparspak MMD). Not ours, not published, and
# optional: both builds detect this directory rather than requiring it. See docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md.
private/

# Copies of the vendored codes GENERATED on demand: retyped to int64 for the width study, and
# hooked to emit the raw elimination order for the amd acceptance test and the benchmark's AMDraw
# column. Generated from private/ and removed by make clean, so that no edited copy of vendored
# code can drift from the original unnoticed. See tools/hook_amd.py, which both consumers call.
experiments/ordering/amd_int64.cpp
experiments/ordering/mmd_int64.cpp
experiments/ordering/amd_raw.cpp
benchmarks/ordering/amd_raw.cpp

# Matrices downloaded from the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection, and the collection's index file.
# Not ours, large, and reproducible from benchmarks/matrices/ssget.py, which is what is committed
# instead. The layout is data/<Group>/<name>.mtx, the collection's own, so a file says where it
# came from.
data/

*.pdf

REPO_MAP.md
reference/

.claude/

tmp/
